WEBVTT

1
00:01:09,583 --> 00:01:11,208
<i>People always ask me</i>

2
00:01:12,625 --> 00:01:15,375
<i>what's so exciting</i>
<i>about riding a motorcycle.</i>

3
00:01:16,541 --> 00:01:18,416
<i>It's noisy.</i>

4
00:01:18,500 --> 00:01:20,250
<i>It's dangerous.</i>

5
00:01:21,500 --> 00:01:24,416
<i>What does a street racer want?</i>

6
00:01:39,666 --> 00:01:40,958
<i>What are we looking for?</i>

7
00:01:44,416 --> 00:01:45,958
<i>What do we want?</i>

8
00:01:51,666 --> 00:01:53,625
{\an8}<i>Aren't we afraid of death?</i>

9
00:01:58,416 --> 00:02:00,125
<i>Aren't we tired of making a scene?</i>

10
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:12,291
<i>For me, I would say…</i>

11
00:02:13,875 --> 00:02:15,000
SALAHUDDIN ROAD

12
00:02:17,250 --> 00:02:19,291
<i>No. We're not tired of it.</i>

13
00:02:39,083 --> 00:02:42,125
<i>My first love is speed.</i>

14
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:46,375
<i>Once you twist the throttle</i>
<i>until your hands are numb,</i>

15
00:02:47,916 --> 00:02:50,875
<i>once you see how</i>
<i>the world turns to a blur…</i>

16
00:02:56,791 --> 00:02:58,958
<i>all of your problems</i>

17
00:03:00,541 --> 00:03:01,708
<i>will go away.</i>

18
00:04:46,875 --> 00:04:49,916
If you're not happy, then start a game!

19
00:04:50,000 --> 00:04:53,583
Tell your stupid boss, Boy,

20
00:04:53,666 --> 00:04:56,083
don't send his goons
to bother me at night.

21
00:04:56,166 --> 00:04:59,333
Cocky, are we? You're Azam, right?

22
00:04:59,416 --> 00:05:02,041
If your bike is that great,
what are you waiting for?

23
00:05:03,000 --> 00:05:04,750
Do I look scared?

24
00:05:05,583 --> 00:05:06,833
Just you wait.

25
00:05:07,333 --> 00:05:09,125
Wait?

26
00:05:10,250 --> 00:05:11,958
You're the scaredy-cat, you goon!

27
00:05:13,166 --> 00:05:14,000
Idiot.

28
00:05:19,416 --> 00:05:21,458
Standing in the street? Are you blind?

29
00:05:31,666 --> 00:05:33,875
Yes, I am. So what?

30
00:05:51,833 --> 00:05:55,750
SULTAN ISMAIL PARK

31
00:06:10,291 --> 00:06:11,666
<i>Do you really live here?</i>

32
00:06:15,208 --> 00:06:18,083
I am blind. I can't see.

33
00:06:19,250 --> 00:06:20,833
How do you know this is your flat?

34
00:06:20,916 --> 00:06:23,375
What if I had taken you elsewhere?

35
00:06:24,125 --> 00:06:26,375
What if I sell you? You wouldn't know.

36
00:06:29,666 --> 00:06:31,416
That's a motorcycle lot, right?

37
00:06:34,958 --> 00:06:36,250
There are flags up there.

38
00:06:37,250 --> 00:06:39,083
I can see a bit in the day.

39
00:06:39,583 --> 00:06:40,750
Harder at night.

40
00:06:44,541 --> 00:06:45,791
Your loss.

41
00:06:45,875 --> 00:06:48,208
You can't see my handsome face.

42
00:06:53,041 --> 00:06:54,166
Hey.

43
00:06:55,291 --> 00:06:58,500
I'm sorry that I nearly hit you earlier.

44
00:06:58,583 --> 00:06:59,583
It's okay.

45
00:07:00,208 --> 00:07:01,625
Thank you for bringing me home.

46
00:07:10,458 --> 00:07:12,625
Hey!

47
00:07:13,458 --> 00:07:14,375
You…

48
00:07:15,833 --> 00:07:18,166
That was close.

49
00:07:23,083 --> 00:07:24,125
Back from work?

50
00:07:24,625 --> 00:07:27,541
Yes. At a hardware store near here.

51
00:07:28,791 --> 00:07:30,750
But why are you following me?

52
00:07:35,125 --> 00:07:38,083
Nothing. I just don't want you to fall.

53
00:07:40,875 --> 00:07:42,875
I use these stairs every day.

54
00:07:49,125 --> 00:07:51,333
A blind person
can work at a hardware shop?

55
00:07:51,833 --> 00:07:55,291
What? Are we only qualified
to be a masseuse?

56
00:07:57,125 --> 00:07:58,291
It's just a question.

57
00:08:01,666 --> 00:08:04,625
Ratna? You're home late today.

58
00:08:04,708 --> 00:08:06,125
Who is this?

59
00:08:06,208 --> 00:08:09,041
A friend, Sis Mila.
He just had an accident.

60
00:08:09,125 --> 00:08:12,291
Goodness. Wait there.
I'll get some medicine.

61
00:08:21,250 --> 00:08:22,125
Come on in.

62
00:08:22,208 --> 00:08:24,833
No, thanks. I have to go now.

63
00:08:25,333 --> 00:08:28,208
Just come in.
You're not a murderer, are you?

64
00:08:31,416 --> 00:08:32,458
No.

65
00:08:41,916 --> 00:08:43,125
My name is Azam.

66
00:08:46,041 --> 00:08:47,083
Ratna.

67
00:08:48,916 --> 00:08:50,083
Ratna…

68
00:09:02,583 --> 00:09:03,833
Don't move.

69
00:09:09,708 --> 00:09:11,333
Your parents are not home?

70
00:09:11,958 --> 00:09:13,666
My dad is in Johor Bahru.

71
00:09:14,333 --> 00:09:15,625
My mum has passed.

72
00:09:20,375 --> 00:09:22,166
Aren't you afraid of being alone?

73
00:09:23,291 --> 00:09:25,500
There could be ghosts. Or <i>Orang Minyak.</i>

74
00:09:37,416 --> 00:09:39,375
Okay. Done.

75
00:10:03,125 --> 00:10:05,708
<i>Can't you answer your phone?</i>

76
00:10:06,208 --> 00:10:08,041
<i>The pipes are in. It'll be done tonight.</i>

77
00:10:08,125 --> 00:10:09,250
Seriously?

78
00:10:09,333 --> 00:10:11,708
-<i>Hurry!</i>
-Wait there. I'll be there soon.

79
00:10:12,666 --> 00:10:13,583
Ratna.

80
00:10:14,458 --> 00:10:16,666
I have to go now.

81
00:10:18,333 --> 00:10:19,333
Thank you.

82
00:10:19,916 --> 00:10:21,958
For nursing me and all that.

83
00:10:22,458 --> 00:10:24,541
Okay. Thank you.

84
00:10:26,458 --> 00:10:27,416
Peace be upon you.

85
00:10:44,541 --> 00:10:45,375
Azam!

86
00:10:52,125 --> 00:10:53,166
What is it?

87
00:10:57,750 --> 00:10:58,833
It's nothing.

88
00:11:04,625 --> 00:11:06,500
-Zero-one-seven…
-Wait!

89
00:11:09,375 --> 00:11:13,000
Two-seven-seven,
grandma falls from heaven.

90
00:11:15,375 --> 00:11:16,750
Come on.

91
00:11:17,250 --> 00:11:19,291
-No need then.
-Do you want it or not?

92
00:11:19,375 --> 00:11:21,041
Of course I do.

93
00:11:21,125 --> 00:11:23,708
Okay. Today will be the last

94
00:11:23,791 --> 00:11:28,833
and final day
for the Red Leo exhaust sale.

95
00:11:28,916 --> 00:11:31,833
Look closely. I will show it to you.

96
00:11:31,916 --> 00:11:34,333
One more thing. If you buy it today,

97
00:11:35,125 --> 00:11:36,291
you'll get a free sticker.

98
00:11:36,375 --> 00:11:38,833
You won't get it tomorrow.

99
00:11:39,833 --> 00:11:41,416
Okay. I have to go now.

100
00:11:41,500 --> 00:11:44,250
If anything, DM me.

101
00:11:44,333 --> 00:11:46,083
Straight up!

102
00:11:47,333 --> 00:11:49,833
That's enough of that.

103
00:11:51,083 --> 00:11:52,000
Hey.

104
00:11:52,500 --> 00:11:54,500
You're just a coolie of the workshop.

105
00:11:55,583 --> 00:11:56,875
Come and work on this bike.

106
00:12:00,291 --> 00:12:01,375
Azam.

107
00:12:02,375 --> 00:12:05,791
Boy's goons are angry.
What did you tell Kutu?

108
00:12:05,875 --> 00:12:07,958
I saw the comments on my livestream.

109
00:12:08,458 --> 00:12:10,541
Let them say whatever.

110
00:12:10,625 --> 00:12:12,000
What are we waiting for?

111
00:12:12,916 --> 00:12:14,125
Let's go.

112
00:12:19,416 --> 00:12:22,041
-Are you ready?
-Show it.

113
00:12:22,125 --> 00:12:26,416
Announcing the arrival of Your Majesty…

114
00:12:39,833 --> 00:12:41,541
My God!

115
00:12:56,458 --> 00:12:57,500
Azam.

116
00:12:58,458 --> 00:12:59,916
Are you sure about racing with this?

117
00:13:00,000 --> 00:13:01,375
It's too valuable.

118
00:13:01,875 --> 00:13:05,791
If you sell it, you can get
around RM20,000 to RM30,000.

119
00:13:06,666 --> 00:13:09,750
You know how bad
this illegal stuff is, right?

120
00:13:10,250 --> 00:13:12,333
Anything happens, you'll end up dead.

121
00:13:12,416 --> 00:13:13,541
Come on.

122
00:13:13,625 --> 00:13:15,416
Just say you want to race.

123
00:13:16,000 --> 00:13:17,875
This baldy!

124
00:13:17,958 --> 00:13:19,500
Shut up.

125
00:13:20,416 --> 00:13:21,416
Jimmy.

126
00:13:22,041 --> 00:13:25,458
I will not die as long as
we haven't achieved our target.

127
00:13:26,666 --> 00:13:29,458
How long will you use your mum's Kriss?

128
00:13:29,541 --> 00:13:32,625
Doing deliveries all day
and the workshop at night.

129
00:13:32,708 --> 00:13:34,583
Repairing bikes.

130
00:13:34,666 --> 00:13:36,291
For how long?

131
00:13:36,375 --> 00:13:39,416
Jimmy, this guy's sister's college fee

132
00:13:39,500 --> 00:13:43,375
is about RM40,000. That's too much!

133
00:13:45,208 --> 00:13:48,791
Didn't you tell me that one day

134
00:13:48,875 --> 00:13:50,916
you'll have your own workshop?

135
00:13:53,625 --> 00:13:56,750
How long do you want to work
as a mechanic here, Mat Jet?

136
00:13:57,625 --> 00:14:01,166
The thing is, if we start a game,

137
00:14:01,666 --> 00:14:05,041
we only need to win RM20,000
three to four times.

138
00:14:05,666 --> 00:14:09,416
I'm sure all your problems

139
00:14:09,500 --> 00:14:11,791
and Mat Jet's problems will be resolved.

140
00:14:16,000 --> 00:14:17,208
Even mine too.

141
00:14:19,791 --> 00:14:21,666
That's our target.

142
00:14:21,750 --> 00:14:22,958
Trust me.

143
00:14:24,250 --> 00:14:25,500
This bike…

144
00:14:27,583 --> 00:14:29,166
will change our lives.

145
00:14:30,291 --> 00:14:31,375
Trust me.

146
00:14:44,041 --> 00:14:46,041
Mat Jet, help Jimmy.

147
00:15:01,708 --> 00:15:04,166
CUP PRIX GEM
A HOPE FOR MALAYSIA

148
00:15:08,000 --> 00:15:10,666
Along, what are you doing? Get up now.

149
00:15:10,750 --> 00:15:12,208
Get up!

150
00:15:12,708 --> 00:15:14,750
Get up. Sit over there.

151
00:15:14,833 --> 00:15:16,583
Why are you eating like this?

152
00:15:20,250 --> 00:15:21,333
Sit here.

153
00:15:25,750 --> 00:15:28,583
What is this? You're making a mess.

154
00:15:28,666 --> 00:15:31,583
I told you, tell me if you need to eat.

155
00:15:31,666 --> 00:15:33,375
I will get it for you.

156
00:15:35,333 --> 00:15:36,208
Angah.

157
00:15:37,791 --> 00:15:40,666
Angah, don't you have any money coming in?

158
00:15:40,750 --> 00:15:41,625
Anything?

159
00:15:43,875 --> 00:15:44,750
What do you mean?

160
00:15:44,833 --> 00:15:47,916
Lend me some, Angah.

161
00:15:48,000 --> 00:15:49,000
Just a bit.

162
00:15:50,458 --> 00:15:52,208
If you're planning to buy drugs,

163
00:15:52,291 --> 00:15:54,583
you can ask me a thousand times,

164
00:15:54,666 --> 00:15:57,916
or cry yourself a river,
you will still get none.

165
00:15:59,541 --> 00:16:02,541
Angah. Angah.

166
00:16:05,625 --> 00:16:06,708
Angah.

167
00:16:20,500 --> 00:16:22,791
It's only because I feel sorry for you

168
00:16:24,541 --> 00:16:26,083
that I promise you

169
00:16:29,291 --> 00:16:30,833
we will leave this place.

170
00:16:55,458 --> 00:16:56,458
Is Arash okay?

171
00:16:57,125 --> 00:16:59,875
Who knows? I don't want to think about it.

172
00:17:00,375 --> 00:17:01,458
It's tiring.

173
00:17:02,125 --> 00:17:05,041
No need to think.
Let's just think about this.

174
00:17:07,208 --> 00:17:08,708
Where did you get this?

175
00:17:09,541 --> 00:17:10,458
My mum found it.

176
00:17:11,041 --> 00:17:13,750
-You look the same.
-Haven't aged a bit.

177
00:17:16,625 --> 00:17:17,750
Azam.

178
00:17:20,041 --> 00:17:22,833
If you seriously
want to race with the bike,

179
00:17:24,791 --> 00:17:26,250
how about you let me join you?

180
00:17:27,791 --> 00:17:30,041
I mean, if we do it together,

181
00:17:30,541 --> 00:17:32,333
the faster we will get to our target.

182
00:17:35,125 --> 00:17:37,375
You're still jerky on the clutch.

183
00:17:38,041 --> 00:17:41,541
I am not trying to criticize you.
You know you're not good at it.

184
00:17:42,125 --> 00:17:46,041
You know how dangerous it is. Don't do it.

185
00:17:47,583 --> 00:17:51,208
It's just that you're doing
everything on your own.

186
00:17:51,291 --> 00:17:52,708
Remember what we used to say?

187
00:17:52,791 --> 00:17:54,625
We will conquer KL together.

188
00:17:56,458 --> 00:17:58,750
But that was when we'd race on bicycles.

189
00:17:58,833 --> 00:18:01,500
Come on, man. See you tomorrow.

190
00:18:02,166 --> 00:18:03,250
Ciao.

191
00:18:20,291 --> 00:18:21,416
SORRY, I AM BLIND
RING THE BELL TO PAY

192
00:18:31,291 --> 00:18:33,375
-How much?
-That's RM40.

193
00:18:34,125 --> 00:18:35,125
Wait.

194
00:18:36,875 --> 00:18:39,125
<i>Received. RM40.</i>

195
00:18:39,208 --> 00:18:40,791
-Thank you.
-You're welcome.

196
00:19:03,041 --> 00:19:04,125
-Hey!
-It's okay…

197
00:19:04,208 --> 00:19:07,583
Relax. It's me. Azam.

198
00:19:08,500 --> 00:19:09,708
What is that you're drawing?

199
00:19:10,750 --> 00:19:12,000
What are you doing here?

200
00:19:12,750 --> 00:19:14,208
Don't be mad.

201
00:19:14,875 --> 00:19:16,000
Am I bothering you?

202
00:19:18,125 --> 00:19:22,166
I'm here to invite you for lunch.

203
00:19:25,166 --> 00:19:26,333
What time will you be off work?

204
00:19:28,291 --> 00:19:29,583
In a moment.

205
00:19:44,916 --> 00:19:46,083
What are you looking at?

206
00:19:46,791 --> 00:19:49,083
You need a car for a date, right?

207
00:19:49,166 --> 00:19:52,291
Come on. Don't be a brat.

208
00:19:54,083 --> 00:19:55,333
Hey.

209
00:19:55,416 --> 00:19:56,416
Hang on.

210
00:20:05,166 --> 00:20:06,708
Send photo to Sis Milah.

211
00:20:08,291 --> 00:20:10,875
Sis Milah, I'm going out with Azam.

212
00:20:10,958 --> 00:20:12,250
I'll be home a bit late.

213
00:20:13,250 --> 00:20:15,083
Sis Milah gets worried if I'm home late.

214
00:20:15,916 --> 00:20:16,833
Okay.

215
00:20:26,833 --> 00:20:28,458
This isn't the previous bike, right?

216
00:20:29,166 --> 00:20:30,166
No.

217
00:20:31,625 --> 00:20:33,291
Straighten your head for the helmet.

218
00:20:40,666 --> 00:20:41,500
Get on.

219
00:20:52,583 --> 00:20:54,375
The previous bike is cuter.

220
00:20:55,916 --> 00:20:58,666
But this one is louder!

221
00:21:16,500 --> 00:21:17,958
So, you love to do art?

222
00:21:19,500 --> 00:21:21,916
And you? Street racing?

223
00:21:23,750 --> 00:21:26,750
I can recognize it
from the sound of your bike.

224
00:21:32,416 --> 00:21:33,458
Why?

225
00:21:35,208 --> 00:21:36,458
Do you hate street racers?

226
00:21:37,833 --> 00:21:38,875
Not at all.

227
00:21:39,625 --> 00:21:43,583
But I always hear it on the news.
It's dangerous to ride at high speed.

228
00:21:46,875 --> 00:21:48,000
I don't know.

229
00:21:51,958 --> 00:21:54,541
You won't understand even if I tell you.

230
00:21:58,000 --> 00:21:59,125
It's okay not to understand.

231
00:22:00,208 --> 00:22:01,500
Just knowing is fine.

232
00:22:11,208 --> 00:22:12,916
My brother was once a racer.

233
00:22:14,916 --> 00:22:16,916
Both legally and illegally.

234
00:22:20,666 --> 00:22:22,750
My parents died when I was a child.

235
00:22:25,041 --> 00:22:28,166
So, my brother became my guardian.

236
00:22:29,166 --> 00:22:30,708
But that was then.

237
00:22:33,000 --> 00:22:34,333
After his accident,

238
00:22:37,291 --> 00:22:38,541
he started using drugs.

239
00:22:40,750 --> 00:22:42,125
He's different now.

240
00:22:47,666 --> 00:22:51,375
But the thing is, I have to race.

241
00:22:51,458 --> 00:22:54,958
That's the only way
for someone like me to make money.

242
00:22:59,125 --> 00:23:03,041
You know, my late father
has a house in Perlis.

243
00:23:04,250 --> 00:23:06,375
When I have enough money,

244
00:23:06,875 --> 00:23:08,708
I want to repair the place.

245
00:23:10,708 --> 00:23:12,291
I will take Arash there.

246
00:23:13,291 --> 00:23:14,583
Away from KL.

247
00:23:30,125 --> 00:23:31,875
Get on the bike. Wear your helmet.

248
00:23:36,833 --> 00:23:37,958
Boy.

249
00:23:49,500 --> 00:23:52,875
Kutu, was this the guy
who talked about me?

250
00:23:52,958 --> 00:23:53,791
The very same.

251
00:23:54,625 --> 00:23:58,375
Boy, do your parents allow you
to be out this late?

252
00:24:01,541 --> 00:24:06,125
Do you think Boy is scared
of this new bike of yours?

253
00:24:07,666 --> 00:24:09,791
He is. Not me.

254
00:24:11,916 --> 00:24:13,166
I want to start a game.

255
00:24:15,541 --> 00:24:16,583
Fifty.

256
00:24:17,291 --> 00:24:19,166
Fifty thousand?

257
00:24:20,333 --> 00:24:22,000
Do you think I'm stupid?

258
00:24:22,791 --> 00:24:24,958
Just race with your family, Boy.

259
00:24:25,791 --> 00:24:27,708
You're not like me. You have your dad.

260
00:24:28,208 --> 00:24:30,458
I don't. Mine is dead.

261
00:24:31,458 --> 00:24:33,958
You can ask for money from daddy.
You know why?

262
00:24:34,041 --> 00:24:35,541
Because your dad is stupid.

263
00:24:37,041 --> 00:24:38,208
Just like you!

264
00:24:43,333 --> 00:24:45,958
Boy, you can't just ignore it.

265
00:24:48,708 --> 00:24:50,416
What are you waiting for? Go after him!

266
00:24:52,541 --> 00:24:55,250
Hey, Zahar. Use your bike, you idiot!

267
00:25:20,958 --> 00:25:22,250
Who are those people?

268
00:25:22,833 --> 00:25:24,125
What do they want?

269
00:25:25,125 --> 00:25:28,125
It's nothing, Ratna. Just some idiots.

270
00:25:29,208 --> 00:25:30,458
Don't worry, alright?

271
00:25:31,416 --> 00:25:35,083
If anything happens,
I will protect you. Okay?

272
00:26:11,000 --> 00:26:14,291
Hey, Jimmy. Why are you lying down?

273
00:26:15,250 --> 00:26:16,958
Who's going to work on the bike?

274
00:26:17,458 --> 00:26:18,583
Huh?

275
00:26:18,666 --> 00:26:21,125
I went from Dengkil to Gombak,

276
00:26:21,208 --> 00:26:23,458
and turned back to Cheras to do delivery.

277
00:26:24,041 --> 00:26:25,750
Mum's Kriss is in dire condition.

278
00:26:26,416 --> 00:26:27,583
Give me some space, man.

279
00:26:35,208 --> 00:26:37,333
<i>I am looking for a purple RXZ.</i>

280
00:26:37,416 --> 00:26:39,791
<i>Plate number, KEU 51.</i>

281
00:26:40,291 --> 00:26:41,791
Azam has caused a problem.

282
00:26:41,875 --> 00:26:44,000
<i>This rascal is called Azam.</i>

283
00:26:44,583 --> 00:26:45,916
{\an8}<i>He has a workshop.</i>

284
00:26:46,000 --> 00:26:49,125
{\an8}<i>Find it, and I will give you a bonus.</i>
<i>How about that?</i>

285
00:26:52,625 --> 00:26:53,958
Call Azam.

286
00:27:04,000 --> 00:27:05,583
What now?

287
00:27:10,708 --> 00:27:11,833
Here.

288
00:27:17,458 --> 00:27:19,208
Now it's better. Here.

289
00:27:19,291 --> 00:27:21,083
It's okay. Keep it for now.

290
00:27:24,291 --> 00:27:25,666
Here.

291
00:27:32,791 --> 00:27:33,625
A whistle.

292
00:27:35,291 --> 00:27:39,041
If someone is bothering you
or you fall down or something,

293
00:27:39,125 --> 00:27:42,000
just blow the whistle,
and I will be there.

294
00:27:44,333 --> 00:27:46,208
Yes, like that.

295
00:27:46,291 --> 00:27:47,583
I can be a referee.

296
00:27:47,666 --> 00:27:49,666
You can show the yellow card too.

297
00:27:52,291 --> 00:27:53,291
Thank you, Azam.

298
00:27:54,291 --> 00:27:55,583
I have to go now.

299
00:27:56,666 --> 00:27:57,833
Be careful.

300
00:28:06,500 --> 00:28:07,458
Azam.

301
00:28:08,916 --> 00:28:10,333
This wasn't a date, right?

302
00:28:11,666 --> 00:28:13,583
You need a car for a date, right?

303
00:28:15,916 --> 00:28:17,583
Okay. Goodbye!

304
00:28:18,500 --> 00:28:19,541
Goodbye.

305
00:28:37,541 --> 00:28:39,875
-Mat Jet.
<i>-Too deaf to hear the phone ring?</i>

306
00:28:40,375 --> 00:28:43,208
I was on the bike. Shut up.

307
00:28:43,291 --> 00:28:45,166
-What's up?
<i>-Come home now.</i>

308
00:28:45,250 --> 00:28:47,125
<i>Your house is being surrounded.</i>

309
00:28:49,333 --> 00:28:50,708
Wait for me there.

310
00:29:03,875 --> 00:29:07,291
Peace be upon you!

311
00:29:07,375 --> 00:29:11,041
Azam? Azam!

312
00:29:13,625 --> 00:29:15,916
Jet, if Azam is not here in 10 minutes,

313
00:29:16,000 --> 00:29:17,250
just call the police.

314
00:29:17,333 --> 00:29:21,083
Why would we call the police?
Let's just fight them!

315
00:29:22,625 --> 00:29:24,541
That's stupid!

316
00:29:25,208 --> 00:29:28,250
Boy pummeled a Cheras kid once.
He was in the ICU for a month!

317
00:29:34,708 --> 00:29:38,958
So stupid!

318
00:29:39,458 --> 00:29:41,333
Just eat your pumpkin seed.

319
00:29:41,916 --> 00:29:43,708
This is ridiculous!

320
00:29:47,916 --> 00:29:50,583
Kutu, are you waiting for revelation?

321
00:29:52,750 --> 00:29:54,000
Aye, aye, Chief.

322
00:30:09,458 --> 00:30:10,625
So many of you!

323
00:30:11,125 --> 00:30:12,541
Jimmy! Mat Jet!

324
00:30:13,333 --> 00:30:15,291
What's up? Is there an event?

325
00:30:16,000 --> 00:30:17,333
Boy.

326
00:30:17,416 --> 00:30:20,250
If you missed me,
no need to find me at home.

327
00:30:22,125 --> 00:30:24,625
You do know, right?
I only need to snap my fingers,

328
00:30:24,708 --> 00:30:26,416
and you will be crushed.

329
00:30:28,000 --> 00:30:30,958
I know. But your mutts are awesome.

330
00:30:31,625 --> 00:30:33,000
How much do you make?

331
00:30:33,625 --> 00:30:35,208
Does it come with SOCSO?

332
00:30:36,000 --> 00:30:38,791
Better than your goons.

333
00:30:40,416 --> 00:30:42,458
No balls.

334
00:30:43,291 --> 00:30:44,291
Next weekend.

335
00:30:45,166 --> 00:30:48,041
RXZ Open. RM100,000.

336
00:30:51,583 --> 00:30:54,000
Okay. I promise you I will be there.

337
00:30:54,083 --> 00:30:56,458
Okay? You two, remember my face.

338
00:30:56,541 --> 00:30:58,458
But let's sell your sister first.

339
00:30:59,500 --> 00:31:02,625
Relax, Boy. This can be discussed.

340
00:31:19,833 --> 00:31:22,791
Hey, you bum. Do you think I care?

341
00:31:22,875 --> 00:31:24,416
You're just a hick.

342
00:31:25,208 --> 00:31:29,166
People only respect you
because you are Arash's brother.

343
00:31:29,666 --> 00:31:31,208
But what happened to him?

344
00:31:32,208 --> 00:31:33,458
He's an addict, right?

345
00:31:33,958 --> 00:31:35,125
Just a scum, right?

346
00:31:36,333 --> 00:31:37,666
Come to the game,

347
00:31:40,125 --> 00:31:42,625
or I will kill that addict.

348
00:31:59,375 --> 00:32:00,583
What now, Azam?

349
00:32:01,791 --> 00:32:03,541
What do you mean "what now"?

350
00:32:04,250 --> 00:32:06,875
None of you helped when they pummeled me.

351
00:32:07,500 --> 00:32:09,833
I think we should leave KL.

352
00:32:11,250 --> 00:32:13,166
Where can we get RM100,000?

353
00:32:17,208 --> 00:32:18,708
But what if I win?

354
00:32:19,208 --> 00:32:20,833
If you win.

355
00:32:21,583 --> 00:32:22,750
If you don't?

356
00:32:23,416 --> 00:32:24,875
You'll be a slave.

357
00:32:24,958 --> 00:32:27,000
I am confident I'll win.

358
00:32:27,083 --> 00:32:29,208
I don't want you to regret it.

359
00:32:33,208 --> 00:32:34,250
Jet.

360
00:32:35,833 --> 00:32:37,125
Use the workshop's money.

361
00:32:37,708 --> 00:32:39,291
Are you serious?

362
00:32:39,375 --> 00:32:42,791
I don't mind,
but it still won't be enough.

363
00:32:43,541 --> 00:32:44,958
I have my savings.

364
00:32:46,333 --> 00:32:48,791
Put in your savings as well,
it'll be enough.

365
00:32:48,875 --> 00:32:50,875
I don't have much, Azam.

366
00:32:51,583 --> 00:32:53,166
Let alone Mat Jet.

367
00:33:02,083 --> 00:33:03,416
The bike as well.

368
00:33:11,583 --> 00:33:12,666
What say you?

369
00:33:16,791 --> 00:33:17,875
DAD'S HOUSE REPAIR

370
00:33:17,958 --> 00:33:19,750
ROOF RM7K, DOOR X FOUR RM2.5K,
WIRING RM5K

371
00:33:19,833 --> 00:33:21,500
PLUMBING RM4K - FLOORING RM10K

372
00:33:21,583 --> 00:33:23,041
ARASH'S HOSPITAL BILL RM20,000

373
00:33:28,416 --> 00:33:29,500
<i>Next weekend.</i>

374
00:33:29,583 --> 00:33:32,583
RXZ Open. RM100,000.

375
00:33:33,083 --> 00:33:35,833
If you lose, you'll be a slave.

376
00:34:06,083 --> 00:34:07,291
Where did you get the money?

377
00:34:10,000 --> 00:34:11,500
Did you sell your trophy?

378
00:34:12,958 --> 00:34:14,875
You sold it, didn't you? I'm asking you!

379
00:34:14,958 --> 00:34:17,833
-Get up!
-My leg hurts. My leg hurts!

380
00:34:17,916 --> 00:34:20,750
-You sold your trophy, didn't you?
-No…

381
00:34:20,833 --> 00:34:22,125
How could you sell it?

382
00:34:22,208 --> 00:34:24,041
Are you stupid?

383
00:34:24,125 --> 00:34:25,791
Shut up, you scum!

384
00:34:25,875 --> 00:34:27,375
You're the scum!

385
00:34:29,583 --> 00:34:31,916
Do you think you're so great?

386
00:34:32,000 --> 00:34:33,916
So great that you can teach me?

387
00:34:34,000 --> 00:34:36,500
I took care of you.

388
00:34:41,083 --> 00:34:43,416
You and I are no different.

389
00:34:43,916 --> 00:34:46,958
What did you say?
Repeat that again, Along.

390
00:34:48,916 --> 00:34:50,541
Repeat that. What did you say?

391
00:34:52,916 --> 00:34:54,416
What's the difference?

392
00:34:54,916 --> 00:34:57,625
Between you racing illegally
and me doing drugs?

393
00:35:07,875 --> 00:35:09,041
Tell me.

394
00:35:09,958 --> 00:35:12,916
That thing you do can kill you.

395
00:35:13,791 --> 00:35:15,958
This thing I do can kill me.

396
00:35:16,458 --> 00:35:17,750
Same difference, Angah.

397
00:35:18,458 --> 00:35:21,750
I have to race.

398
00:35:21,833 --> 00:35:23,500
I have to make money.

399
00:35:23,583 --> 00:35:26,708
So that I can repair
Dad's house in the village!

400
00:35:27,208 --> 00:35:28,333
Can't you think?

401
00:35:28,416 --> 00:35:32,166
Your stupid friends
won't be able to find you anymore!

402
00:35:32,250 --> 00:35:36,000
You will be healthy again.
Can you understand that?

403
00:35:38,083 --> 00:35:39,000
Healthy?

404
00:35:40,041 --> 00:35:41,333
Healthy, I see.

405
00:35:41,416 --> 00:35:43,375
Did I say I want to be healthy?

406
00:35:43,875 --> 00:35:45,916
Did I say that, Angah?

407
00:35:46,708 --> 00:35:48,083
I just want my stuff.

408
00:35:48,166 --> 00:35:52,583
This. I just want my stuff!

409
00:35:52,666 --> 00:35:53,750
Do you even understand?

410
00:35:56,000 --> 00:35:57,583
Drats.

411
00:36:10,250 --> 00:36:11,583
Along.

412
00:36:13,208 --> 00:36:14,541
I'm tired.

413
00:36:16,250 --> 00:36:20,250
I am so tired of carrying
a burden like you.

414
00:36:24,208 --> 00:36:25,791
From now on,

415
00:36:26,833 --> 00:36:29,041
you're no longer my brother.

416
00:36:33,250 --> 00:36:34,375
Angah.

417
00:36:36,875 --> 00:36:38,750
Slumdogs like us?

418
00:36:40,041 --> 00:36:44,166
We'll be a nuisance for life.

419
00:36:46,458 --> 00:36:47,875
You remember that.

420
00:36:55,500 --> 00:36:57,166
It's all spilled, Angah.

421
00:37:46,541 --> 00:37:47,708
Jet.

422
00:37:47,791 --> 00:37:50,375
If Azam loses, where will you go?

423
00:37:52,000 --> 00:37:55,416
They said that tickets to Maldives
are cheap right now.

424
00:37:57,458 --> 00:37:58,625
What will you do in Maldives?

425
00:37:59,375 --> 00:38:00,458
Become a mechanic.

426
00:38:00,958 --> 00:38:02,125
Idiot.

427
00:38:02,625 --> 00:38:03,791
A mechanic?

428
00:38:03,875 --> 00:38:06,458
-Hey, Azam.
-Azam…

429
00:38:06,541 --> 00:38:08,916
I've been setting the bike up for a week.

430
00:38:09,000 --> 00:38:10,791
It's in perfect condition.

431
00:38:30,041 --> 00:38:31,250
Azam.

432
00:38:31,333 --> 00:38:34,416
Go for a test ride
instead of meeting your girl.

433
00:38:35,291 --> 00:38:36,791
The game is tonight.

434
00:38:36,875 --> 00:38:39,166
I know. The bike is all set up right?

435
00:38:40,916 --> 00:38:42,041
See you tonight.

436
00:38:52,791 --> 00:38:54,458
Don't forget tonight!

437
00:39:04,625 --> 00:39:06,916
I have a bad feeling about this.

438
00:39:09,833 --> 00:39:11,666
So, the Maldives tickets are cheap?

439
00:39:13,000 --> 00:39:14,041
Why?

440
00:39:14,541 --> 00:39:16,583
I told you, you buffoon!

441
00:39:27,708 --> 00:39:29,333
BLIND RATNA

442
00:39:37,041 --> 00:39:37,958
Who are you?

443
00:39:39,041 --> 00:39:40,125
Where is Ratna?

444
00:39:55,041 --> 00:39:56,083
Azam, right?

445
00:39:57,250 --> 00:39:58,166
Yes.

446
00:39:58,833 --> 00:40:00,375
You took Ratna on a bike ride?

447
00:40:02,166 --> 00:40:03,125
Yes.

448
00:40:07,833 --> 00:40:09,166
I don't mind.

449
00:40:11,333 --> 00:40:12,458
But…

450
00:40:13,875 --> 00:40:15,291
Can you help me?

451
00:40:16,708 --> 00:40:18,000
Help you?

452
00:40:19,375 --> 00:40:21,791
Please tell Ratna to come home.

453
00:40:25,166 --> 00:40:26,375
But why?

454
00:40:27,791 --> 00:40:29,375
Why aren't you living with her?

455
00:40:36,083 --> 00:40:40,416
{\an8}<i>That night was</i>
<i>the biggest mistake of my life.</i>

456
00:40:43,500 --> 00:40:45,833
-Get my medicine.
-Mum?

457
00:40:49,250 --> 00:40:50,083
Mum!

458
00:40:57,000 --> 00:40:58,333
Mum.

459
00:41:00,125 --> 00:41:03,250
Mum, wake up.

460
00:41:07,500 --> 00:41:08,666
<i>I made a mistake</i>

461
00:41:09,666 --> 00:41:11,958
<i>by not looking after my wife and daughter.</i>

462
00:41:13,208 --> 00:41:15,166
Ratna wouldn't forgive me.

463
00:41:17,958 --> 00:41:19,625
But maybe you can help me.

464
00:41:31,541 --> 00:41:32,791
Ratna.

465
00:41:36,583 --> 00:41:37,500
Ratna.

466
00:41:39,875 --> 00:41:40,916
Ratna.

467
00:41:42,583 --> 00:41:43,875
Ratna!

468
00:41:43,958 --> 00:41:46,833
Sir, it's fine. I'll go see her.

469
00:41:46,916 --> 00:41:48,791
-Ratna.
-Let me instead.

470
00:41:48,875 --> 00:41:50,166
She's my daughter.

471
00:41:51,166 --> 00:41:53,041
Sorry for having to say this.

472
00:41:54,291 --> 00:41:55,458
If it were me,

473
00:41:56,083 --> 00:41:58,583
and my dad left me, a blind person,

474
00:41:59,083 --> 00:42:02,625
to live with a mum with heart disease,
and she passed away,

475
00:42:03,875 --> 00:42:05,083
do you think…

476
00:42:05,916 --> 00:42:07,625
I would forgive my dad?

477
00:42:07,708 --> 00:42:08,791
Who are you?

478
00:42:09,541 --> 00:42:12,208
Do you think I care
what a slumdog like you thinks?

479
00:42:19,083 --> 00:42:20,083
Ratna.

480
00:42:23,250 --> 00:42:25,833
Ratna, why didn't you answer my calls?

481
00:42:34,916 --> 00:42:36,666
<i>Listen up, everybody.</i>

482
00:42:36,750 --> 00:42:39,416
{\an8}<i>I am looking for a purple RXZ.</i>

483
00:42:39,500 --> 00:42:42,333
{\an8}<i>Plate number KEU 51.</i>

484
00:42:42,416 --> 00:42:44,625
<i>The rascal is called Azam.</i>

485
00:42:45,208 --> 00:42:46,875
Sis Milah showed me the video.

486
00:42:50,500 --> 00:42:51,833
Are you upset with me?

487
00:42:55,541 --> 00:42:56,541
No.

488
00:42:57,916 --> 00:42:59,916
Sis Milah is worried
that you'll drag me too.

489
00:43:00,500 --> 00:43:02,041
Drag you to where?

490
00:43:03,250 --> 00:43:05,625
It's okay. I will talk to Sis Milah.

491
00:43:11,500 --> 00:43:12,458
Ratna.

492
00:43:13,708 --> 00:43:15,000
Are you going fishing?

493
00:43:23,416 --> 00:43:26,708
Ratna, are you buying a fish?

494
00:43:29,291 --> 00:43:32,083
Or were you upset
that I spoke to your dad?

495
00:43:33,250 --> 00:43:34,541
No.

496
00:43:36,166 --> 00:43:37,583
I just like this place.

497
00:43:38,916 --> 00:43:39,916
It's colourful.

498
00:43:41,750 --> 00:43:42,791
Azam.

499
00:43:44,041 --> 00:43:45,500
It must be strange, right?

500
00:43:46,916 --> 00:43:48,416
I'm blind.

501
00:43:49,333 --> 00:43:51,083
And yet I like to draw.

502
00:43:52,041 --> 00:43:55,541
My mum always said that in life…

503
00:43:56,541 --> 00:44:01,500
You will feel less burdened
once you find what you like.

504
00:44:04,250 --> 00:44:05,958
But I'm blind, Azam.

505
00:44:07,208 --> 00:44:11,208
How can I like something
when I can't see it?

506
00:44:12,250 --> 00:44:13,791
But I see them, Azam.

507
00:44:15,958 --> 00:44:17,541
After my mum died,

508
00:44:18,625 --> 00:44:20,916
I promised myself
I wouldn't be sad anymore.

509
00:44:22,166 --> 00:44:23,416
I want to live,

510
00:44:24,500 --> 00:44:25,916
and I want to be happy.

511
00:44:26,750 --> 00:44:28,875
That's why I decided to draw.

512
00:44:30,708 --> 00:44:32,416
Drawing makes me feel…

513
00:44:35,833 --> 00:44:36,916
alive.

514
00:44:44,750 --> 00:44:46,000
But it's okay.

515
00:44:53,416 --> 00:44:54,833
You might not understand.

516
00:44:58,166 --> 00:44:59,458
It's okay not to understand.

517
00:45:01,250 --> 00:45:02,583
Just knowing is fine.

518
00:45:24,375 --> 00:45:25,708
Where is Azam?

519
00:45:30,875 --> 00:45:32,208
Call him.

520
00:46:20,125 --> 00:46:22,791
Come on!

521
00:46:22,875 --> 00:46:25,083
Are you waiting for a feast?

522
00:46:35,708 --> 00:46:36,750
Ratna.

523
00:46:38,791 --> 00:46:41,458
I do feel sorry for your dad.

524
00:46:42,708 --> 00:46:44,166
A bit guilty too.

525
00:46:47,458 --> 00:46:49,625
You really don't want to forgive him?

526
00:46:56,750 --> 00:46:58,041
In the past,

527
00:46:59,208 --> 00:47:01,333
I loved playing at Dad's hardware store.

528
00:47:03,666 --> 00:47:06,083
That's how I memorized
all the stuff there.

529
00:47:09,125 --> 00:47:13,833
He wanted me to stay put,
so he taught me to draw.

530
00:47:16,875 --> 00:47:18,291
I felt really happy

531
00:47:19,916 --> 00:47:22,041
when Dad praised my drawing.

532
00:47:29,708 --> 00:47:32,083
But he was never there for Mum.

533
00:47:33,833 --> 00:47:37,666
From when she was healthy
to when she was ill.

534
00:47:40,416 --> 00:47:42,333
Dad busied himself with work.

535
00:47:45,666 --> 00:47:46,875
That's why I left.

536
00:47:48,208 --> 00:47:50,125
And stayed in his old flat.

537
00:47:54,333 --> 00:47:55,500
I don't know why,

538
00:47:55,583 --> 00:48:00,583
but I can't stop thinking,
if Dad wasn't around,

539
00:48:02,875 --> 00:48:04,708
maybe Mum and I…

540
00:48:09,750 --> 00:48:11,208
would have been happier.

541
00:48:19,083 --> 00:48:20,375
Ratna, do you know?

542
00:48:22,000 --> 00:48:24,500
The first time I found out
that Arash used drugs,

543
00:48:26,791 --> 00:48:28,250
I was enraged.

544
00:48:29,625 --> 00:48:31,458
I mean, just imagine.

545
00:48:32,166 --> 00:48:33,833
He's like a father to me.

546
00:48:36,875 --> 00:48:39,125
But I still take care of him.

547
00:48:41,250 --> 00:48:44,083
No matter what, he is still Arash.

548
00:48:44,791 --> 00:48:46,208
My hero.

549
00:48:48,541 --> 00:48:50,833
But men are like that.

550
00:48:50,916 --> 00:48:52,208
We're a bit of a fool.

551
00:48:52,791 --> 00:48:54,583
Especially with people we love.

552
00:48:59,000 --> 00:49:00,375
Just relax, okay?

553
00:49:05,000 --> 00:49:08,791
Excuse me. Sorry.
Can you check your phone?

554
00:49:12,958 --> 00:49:14,166
MAT JET 17 CALLS

555
00:49:14,250 --> 00:49:17,250
Thank you. Ratna, I have to go.

556
00:49:17,333 --> 00:49:18,833
You know how to go home?

557
00:49:18,916 --> 00:49:19,916
Okay.

558
00:49:20,625 --> 00:49:23,333
-It's okay. I will look after her.
-Cool!

559
00:49:24,375 --> 00:49:26,208
Are you going to race, Azam?

560
00:49:27,500 --> 00:49:29,166
You still owe me a date.

561
00:49:29,666 --> 00:49:30,500
Be careful.

562
00:49:33,541 --> 00:49:35,875
Ratna, once I win,

563
00:49:35,958 --> 00:49:38,333
I can take you on a date
all the way to London!

564
00:49:41,458 --> 00:49:43,416
-Okay, thank you.
-Good luck.

565
00:49:43,500 --> 00:49:45,875
I will book her a Grab car, okay?

566
00:49:50,208 --> 00:49:53,750
How awful. Your buddy has left you two.

567
00:49:54,333 --> 00:49:56,875
Do you think Azam is afraid of you, Boy?

568
00:50:03,500 --> 00:50:04,333
What did you say?

569
00:50:06,083 --> 00:50:07,208
You vermin.

570
00:50:07,708 --> 00:50:10,375
You and your lollipop bike.

571
00:50:10,458 --> 00:50:11,875
Who do you think you are?

572
00:50:11,958 --> 00:50:15,875
At least that lollipop bike
was bought with my own cash.

573
00:50:15,958 --> 00:50:17,541
You only have daddy's money.

574
00:50:17,625 --> 00:50:19,083
You have a problem with me?

575
00:50:19,791 --> 00:50:20,625
And what's up with you?

576
00:50:43,583 --> 00:50:44,666
What's up?

577
00:50:47,375 --> 00:50:48,625
RM100,000, right?

578
00:51:01,166 --> 00:51:02,416
I'll wager RM70,000.

579
00:51:03,708 --> 00:51:05,208
The rest of it on the bike.

580
00:51:11,500 --> 00:51:13,583
Do you think your bike is RM30,000?

581
00:51:16,666 --> 00:51:18,625
Okay, that's fine.

582
00:51:18,708 --> 00:51:20,416
But poor you.

583
00:51:20,958 --> 00:51:23,208
No money for your brother's drugs.

584
00:51:24,583 --> 00:51:25,750
Get ready.

585
00:51:26,458 --> 00:51:27,750
Guys!

586
00:51:31,208 --> 00:51:33,250
Boy is your racer, right?

587
00:51:36,125 --> 00:51:38,208
Your champion, right?

588
00:51:40,500 --> 00:51:42,125
Tonight,

589
00:51:43,166 --> 00:51:47,125
I will entertain you with one eye closed!

590
00:51:51,166 --> 00:51:53,916
I will eat your sugar daddy!

591
00:51:56,125 --> 00:51:57,291
Boy!

592
00:51:59,166 --> 00:52:01,416
What are we waiting for? Let's start!

593
00:56:18,958 --> 00:56:20,583
A hundred, Azam!

594
00:56:23,416 --> 00:56:24,750
Keep the money safe, Jet.

595
00:56:25,333 --> 00:56:26,416
See that?

596
00:56:28,125 --> 00:56:30,583
Boy, what's your deal?

597
00:56:30,666 --> 00:56:32,125
I'm sorry that you lost.

598
00:56:40,708 --> 00:56:43,041
-Seriously?
-You handle it.

599
00:56:48,458 --> 00:56:50,833
Boy, no need to worry.

600
00:56:51,500 --> 00:56:55,458
Later, daddy will transfer some money.

601
00:57:07,583 --> 00:57:09,041
You know what to do, right?

602
00:57:10,375 --> 00:57:11,708
Did you see Boy's face earlier?

603
00:57:12,208 --> 00:57:13,250
Like a sourpuss.

604
00:57:15,083 --> 00:57:17,708
Okay. We have divided the money.

605
00:57:17,791 --> 00:57:18,875
Everything's okay?

606
00:57:18,958 --> 00:57:20,125
-It is.
-You bet…

607
00:57:20,208 --> 00:57:22,458
Azam, if you have the time,

608
00:57:22,541 --> 00:57:24,125
I think I want a new stock.

609
00:57:24,208 --> 00:57:28,333
You should end it with your girl.
It's getting boring.

610
00:57:28,416 --> 00:57:31,625
No, thanks.
I have something else tomorrow.

611
00:57:31,708 --> 00:57:33,250
Okay. I have to go now.

612
00:57:33,333 --> 00:57:34,291
Peace be upon you.

613
00:57:34,375 --> 00:57:35,416
And you.

614
00:57:36,458 --> 00:57:39,458
This guy is worrying me.
Where is he going with his money?

615
00:57:40,375 --> 00:57:41,541
Massage.

616
00:57:42,583 --> 00:57:43,875
Hurry up!

617
00:57:46,416 --> 00:57:48,291
-Be careful, Jet!
-Be careful…

618
00:57:51,625 --> 00:57:53,583
Azam, you do realize, right?

619
00:57:53,666 --> 00:57:55,916
You have the money now.
You can start anew.

620
00:58:05,666 --> 00:58:08,083
Jimmy, you know, earlier,

621
00:58:08,166 --> 00:58:10,541
Boy's goons, both 125ZR riders,

622
00:58:10,625 --> 00:58:12,916
tried to throw my game during the race.

623
00:58:14,625 --> 00:58:16,583
Don't change the topic.

624
00:58:17,083 --> 00:58:18,416
You're the one who said

625
00:58:18,500 --> 00:58:21,833
that once you got the money,
you would leave with Arash.

626
00:58:21,916 --> 00:58:25,250
You can take Arash
to a private clinic with that.

627
00:58:27,250 --> 00:58:28,875
You're such a spoilsport.

628
00:58:29,541 --> 00:58:32,625
Just tell me you want my bike.
You want to be a racer, right?

629
00:58:33,708 --> 00:58:35,125
Azam.

630
00:58:37,666 --> 00:58:40,250
Of course I want to be a racer, like you.

631
00:58:41,916 --> 00:58:44,125
But I am not great at it.

632
00:58:46,083 --> 00:58:47,125
Azam.

633
00:58:49,958 --> 00:58:51,250
I have an idea.

634
00:58:51,750 --> 00:58:54,291
Before you leave,
how about you train me first?

635
00:59:04,583 --> 00:59:06,375
When did I say I'm leaving?

636
00:59:08,750 --> 00:59:09,666
We'll see about that.

637
00:59:35,416 --> 00:59:36,500
DAD'S HOUSE REPAIR

638
00:59:36,583 --> 00:59:37,708
ROOF RM7K, DOOR X FOUR RM2.5K
WIRING RM5K

639
00:59:37,791 --> 00:59:38,916
PLUMBING RM4K
FLOORING 10K

640
01:00:20,458 --> 01:00:21,625
Ratna!

641
01:00:22,666 --> 01:00:23,791
Ratna!

642
01:00:27,083 --> 01:00:28,250
Ratna!

643
01:00:31,125 --> 01:00:31,958
Ratna!

644
01:00:35,416 --> 01:00:36,625
Ratna!

645
01:00:37,625 --> 01:00:38,833
Ratna!

646
01:00:40,666 --> 01:00:41,958
Ratna.

647
01:00:42,041 --> 01:00:45,000
Wear something nice. Let's go.

648
01:00:54,708 --> 01:00:58,083
Wow. You look pretty.

649
01:01:02,166 --> 01:01:03,208
Here.

650
01:01:05,500 --> 01:01:07,541
-Is this new?
-Yes.

651
01:01:10,625 --> 01:01:13,708
That's why it smells nice. Unlike before.

652
01:01:14,208 --> 01:01:15,875
You are so ungrateful.

653
01:01:18,041 --> 01:01:20,166
-Do you want to try something new?
-What?

654
01:01:22,333 --> 01:01:23,333
This!

655
01:01:26,666 --> 01:01:27,666
Here.

656
01:01:28,166 --> 01:01:29,583
One for me.

657
01:01:31,125 --> 01:01:32,416
And one for you.

658
01:01:35,208 --> 01:01:37,208
When the wind is blowing in your face,

659
01:01:38,083 --> 01:01:39,375
just listen to the music.

660
01:01:40,541 --> 01:01:41,958
And close your eyes.

661
01:01:43,291 --> 01:01:46,875
Trust me.
All of your problems will be gone.

662
01:01:48,333 --> 01:01:49,291
Really.

663
01:01:51,041 --> 01:01:52,750
Your bangs will be ruined.

664
01:01:54,750 --> 01:01:57,125
Let's wear the helmet.
Get your head straight.

665
01:02:02,250 --> 01:02:03,083
Wow!

666
01:02:03,166 --> 01:02:04,958
-Is that okay?
-Yes.

667
01:02:05,041 --> 01:02:06,500
Okay.

668
01:02:06,583 --> 01:02:07,791
Let's go.

669
01:02:21,500 --> 01:02:24,791
Why do I have to close my eyes?
It's not like I can see.

670
01:02:25,750 --> 01:02:27,000
That's true.

671
01:02:28,041 --> 01:02:29,666
You're blind.

672
01:02:31,416 --> 01:02:32,375
Let's go.

673
01:04:15,791 --> 01:04:17,041
Azam.

674
01:04:17,125 --> 01:04:20,666
Azam, answer the phone.

675
01:05:14,250 --> 01:05:15,666
Mum, I have to go now.

676
01:05:15,750 --> 01:05:19,333
Okay. Be careful.
Don't go too fast on that bike.

677
01:05:19,416 --> 01:05:21,250
The maximum is only 200km per hour.

678
01:05:21,333 --> 01:05:23,375
This boy!

679
01:05:23,458 --> 01:05:25,291
-I'm going.
-Be careful.

680
01:05:25,375 --> 01:05:26,625
Make supplication.

681
01:06:23,833 --> 01:06:25,583
Jimmy, my boy.

682
01:06:26,083 --> 01:06:27,250
Ma'am.

683
01:06:27,750 --> 01:06:29,125
That's your son, right?

684
01:06:29,625 --> 01:06:32,375
I have some issues with him.

685
01:06:32,875 --> 01:06:34,958
What is wrong with you?

686
01:06:35,458 --> 01:06:36,750
Aren't you afraid of God?

687
01:06:37,458 --> 01:06:38,875
Jimmy.

688
01:06:42,041 --> 01:06:43,250
Boy!

689
01:06:43,333 --> 01:06:47,458
Boy, that's my mum! Boy!

690
01:06:50,583 --> 01:06:53,875
Jimmy, sorry that I kicked your mum.

691
01:06:58,500 --> 01:07:00,000
Boy.

692
01:07:08,333 --> 01:07:11,500
Boy, I'm sorry.

693
01:07:12,291 --> 01:07:16,416
I'm sorry, Boy. Please.
I will bow down to you.

694
01:07:16,500 --> 01:07:18,041
Boy.

695
01:07:27,750 --> 01:07:29,958
Send my regards to your best friend.

696
01:07:33,208 --> 01:07:34,416
Look carefully.

697
01:07:36,916 --> 01:07:41,166
Boy.

698
01:08:17,416 --> 01:08:19,916
So, will you return to your hometown?

699
01:08:20,625 --> 01:08:22,916
You have enough money
to repair the house, right?

700
01:08:25,208 --> 01:08:26,916
It's not that much.

701
01:08:27,750 --> 01:08:29,208
But I'm still unsure.

702
01:08:32,416 --> 01:08:33,625
Why?

703
01:08:34,750 --> 01:08:36,333
Do you still want to race?

704
01:08:44,708 --> 01:08:45,833
Arash.

705
01:08:48,166 --> 01:08:50,875
Arash can't be helped anymore.

706
01:08:53,208 --> 01:08:55,250
I'm tired of him.

707
01:09:01,375 --> 01:09:02,916
But I have you here.

708
01:09:12,416 --> 01:09:16,333
If I blow this whistle,
you will come, right?

709
01:09:19,375 --> 01:09:20,375
Azam.

710
01:09:22,833 --> 01:09:24,000
Come closer.

711
01:09:25,500 --> 01:09:26,583
What is it?

712
01:09:29,416 --> 01:09:30,500
What is it?

713
01:09:44,083 --> 01:09:45,333
Why are you laughing?

714
01:11:40,500 --> 01:11:41,583
Arash.

715
01:11:50,000 --> 01:11:51,041
Arash.

716
01:11:54,333 --> 01:11:56,583
Arash, don't play around. Wake up.

717
01:11:57,708 --> 01:11:58,541
Arash.

718
01:12:00,625 --> 01:12:01,583
Along.

719
01:12:07,083 --> 01:12:08,541
Along, wake up.

720
01:12:10,041 --> 01:12:11,666
Don't play with me.

721
01:12:25,583 --> 01:12:27,541
Wake up, Along. Please.

722
01:13:33,041 --> 01:13:34,250
Condolences, Azam.

723
01:13:36,500 --> 01:13:38,458
Jet, what happened?

724
01:13:38,958 --> 01:13:40,375
Boy sends his regards.

725
01:13:42,125 --> 01:13:43,125
Azam.

726
01:13:43,208 --> 01:13:44,291
The doctor said,

727
01:13:45,333 --> 01:13:48,500
my arm may not return to how it was.

728
01:13:55,875 --> 01:13:58,250
Why are you moving your stuff?

729
01:14:00,458 --> 01:14:04,458
Azam, I think this is where
I stop being your mechanic.

730
01:14:04,541 --> 01:14:07,375
I called you yesterday. You didn't answer.

731
01:14:11,083 --> 01:14:13,708
Jet. Where is Jimmy?

732
01:14:15,291 --> 01:14:17,166
Boy raided Jimmy's place.

733
01:14:17,250 --> 01:14:19,208
His bike was burned down.

734
01:14:19,291 --> 01:14:21,250
His mum has gone back to the village.

735
01:14:21,750 --> 01:14:24,083
He was badly beaten.

736
01:14:24,791 --> 01:14:25,833
Boy?

737
01:14:27,625 --> 01:14:28,708
Why?

738
01:14:29,250 --> 01:14:31,916
Where are you going?
You want to seek revenge?

739
01:14:32,916 --> 01:14:35,333
You want to be a cripple too? Like Arash?

740
01:14:40,833 --> 01:14:41,916
Jet.

741
01:14:45,125 --> 01:14:46,375
I think…

742
01:14:47,541 --> 01:14:50,291
you should just go stay with your girl.

743
01:14:51,375 --> 01:14:54,083
You love to ruin people's lives, right?

744
01:15:30,250 --> 01:15:31,291
Azam.

745
01:15:36,875 --> 01:15:38,041
Why are you quiet?

746
01:15:38,875 --> 01:15:40,583
You don't want to be friends anymore?

747
01:15:41,166 --> 01:15:42,208
No.

748
01:15:43,291 --> 01:15:44,250
No.

749
01:15:49,166 --> 01:15:50,541
It's just that Arash…

750
01:15:52,125 --> 01:15:53,583
Arash is dead.

751
01:15:56,125 --> 01:15:59,333
Ratna, you don't have to come
find me anymore.

752
01:16:00,666 --> 01:16:02,416
You don't even need to call me.

753
01:16:03,916 --> 01:16:06,791
A street racer like me
will just make life harder for you.

754
01:16:10,875 --> 01:16:11,916
Really?

755
01:16:12,916 --> 01:16:14,250
That's what you think.

756
01:16:15,083 --> 01:16:17,208
When did you ever make life hard for me?

757
01:16:18,875 --> 01:16:20,625
Just listen to me, Ratna.

758
01:16:23,291 --> 01:16:24,916
You're still young.

759
01:16:26,291 --> 01:16:27,458
And you're pretty.

760
01:16:29,541 --> 01:16:31,833
Sooner or later, you will forget me.

761
01:16:55,958 --> 01:16:57,333
I will never forget.

762
01:17:11,416 --> 01:17:12,708
Remember this, Ratna.

763
01:17:15,583 --> 01:17:17,250
I will forget you.

764
01:19:17,500 --> 01:19:18,791
What are you doing here?

765
01:19:27,458 --> 01:19:30,875
You have no right to live.

766
01:19:30,958 --> 01:19:32,833
Jimmy, relax.

767
01:19:33,708 --> 01:19:36,750
I had to save face.
It was my men who wanted to beat you up.

768
01:19:36,833 --> 01:19:37,958
What can I do?

769
01:19:38,458 --> 01:19:40,958
Jimmy, relax.

770
01:19:41,458 --> 01:19:43,875
Okay. How much do you want?
I will pay you.

771
01:19:46,958 --> 01:19:48,791
<i>Send my regards to your best friend.</i>

772
01:19:50,375 --> 01:19:51,375
<i>Watch closely.</i>

773
01:22:20,166 --> 01:22:21,375
Ratna.

774
01:22:22,791 --> 01:22:24,875
I know you hate me.

775
01:22:24,958 --> 01:22:27,958
But can you wait and hear me out first?

776
01:22:30,875 --> 01:22:31,833
Peace be upon you.

777
01:22:31,916 --> 01:22:33,333
And you. Come on in.

778
01:22:34,291 --> 01:22:35,375
Ratna.

779
01:22:36,833 --> 01:22:38,250
Are you well?

780
01:22:38,333 --> 01:22:40,416
Ratna, my name is Sarah.

781
01:22:41,208 --> 01:22:42,875
Your artworks are beautiful.

782
01:22:42,958 --> 01:22:45,208
I know a gallery owner.

783
01:22:45,291 --> 01:22:49,750
They have a lot of artworks
made by people like you.

784
01:22:49,833 --> 01:22:52,958
And they have an art school there.

785
01:22:53,041 --> 01:22:55,458
You can learn how to draw,

786
01:22:55,541 --> 01:22:57,583
and then you can sell all your artwork.

787
01:23:00,083 --> 01:23:01,708
Enough is enough, Ratna.

788
01:23:03,833 --> 01:23:05,458
Don't you care for me?

789
01:23:39,916 --> 01:23:41,333
Hey!

790
01:23:41,958 --> 01:23:43,333
Isn't this Boy's bike?

791
01:23:43,833 --> 01:23:45,500
Tell me. This is Boy's, right?

792
01:23:45,583 --> 01:23:47,125
What did you do to him?

793
01:23:47,208 --> 01:23:49,625
Don't make me go to the police!

794
01:23:53,791 --> 01:23:55,000
Friends!

795
01:24:00,166 --> 01:24:03,625
Whichever one of you
can break this guy's face,

796
01:24:04,833 --> 01:24:06,875
I will reward him RM5,000!

797
01:24:07,541 --> 01:24:09,083
Yes!

798
01:24:16,750 --> 01:24:17,750
Will you accept?

799
01:24:23,458 --> 01:24:24,333
Hey, seriously?

800
01:24:26,083 --> 01:24:27,375
We're friends!

801
01:24:29,416 --> 01:24:32,791
Hey, we're all friends.
Have you guys forgotten that?

802
01:25:09,041 --> 01:25:10,416
Thank you.

803
01:25:17,125 --> 01:25:18,250
Azam!

804
01:25:19,333 --> 01:25:20,416
Azam!

805
01:25:31,500 --> 01:25:32,916
What are you doing here?

806
01:25:35,208 --> 01:25:38,333
Tomorrow morning,
Dad wants me to go with him.

807
01:25:41,583 --> 01:25:42,416
That's good then.

808
01:25:42,500 --> 01:25:44,500
But I don't want to go.

809
01:25:45,958 --> 01:25:47,791
Don't do anything foolish.

810
01:25:51,250 --> 01:25:52,625
What's the matter with you?

811
01:25:52,708 --> 01:25:54,625
You were fine before.

812
01:25:58,166 --> 01:25:59,416
Azam.

813
01:26:00,916 --> 01:26:02,500
You know what I want to say, right?

814
01:26:03,666 --> 01:26:06,583
-Azam, I…
-Ratna, let's not talk about this.

815
01:26:24,375 --> 01:26:25,666
Stay inside, okay?

816
01:26:50,750 --> 01:26:52,083
Where were you, Jimmy?

817
01:27:09,541 --> 01:27:10,750
Well…

818
01:27:12,833 --> 01:27:14,750
You were picking up a disabled chick?

819
01:27:16,125 --> 01:27:18,166
Don't you have sympathy for your mum?

820
01:27:18,250 --> 01:27:20,333
What is it to you?

821
01:27:20,416 --> 01:27:24,708
Mat Jet and I were slaving away
in this place, and you never cared.

822
01:27:25,708 --> 01:27:27,375
Things happen, Jimmy.

823
01:27:28,333 --> 01:27:29,750
What do you want me to do?

824
01:27:32,500 --> 01:27:33,833
You stole Boy's bike.

825
01:27:35,208 --> 01:27:37,125
You hung out with the scums.

826
01:27:37,208 --> 01:27:40,250
-What are you trying to do?
-Scums?

827
01:27:40,750 --> 01:27:43,458
They may be scums, but they respect me.

828
01:27:44,541 --> 01:27:46,125
What are you trying to prove?

829
01:27:48,125 --> 01:27:50,250
-That you're powerful?
-I am.

830
01:27:52,000 --> 01:27:54,500
Tonight. Same street.

831
01:27:54,583 --> 01:27:56,708
I don't want to race with you!

832
01:27:57,958 --> 01:27:59,750
You might have looked down on me.

833
01:28:00,833 --> 01:28:03,125
If you don't want to race with me,

834
01:28:06,875 --> 01:28:09,000
I will make her go mute.

835
01:28:09,750 --> 01:28:10,791
Will you accept?

836
01:28:12,250 --> 01:28:13,250
Hey!

837
01:28:13,333 --> 01:28:16,916
Touch her, and I will smash your face.

838
01:28:19,541 --> 01:28:20,791
You want a race?

839
01:28:21,875 --> 01:28:25,083
If you lose, go back to your mum.

840
01:28:26,041 --> 01:28:27,500
And if you lose?

841
01:28:28,000 --> 01:28:30,875
Burn your bike and kiss my feet.

842
01:28:31,458 --> 01:28:32,625
Okay?

843
01:28:34,666 --> 01:28:36,500
If that will satisfy you…

844
01:28:38,000 --> 01:28:39,333
Okay.

845
01:28:59,875 --> 01:29:01,916
You see what my life is like, right?

846
01:29:03,666 --> 01:29:04,833
Just go home.

847
01:29:07,458 --> 01:29:08,500
Leave.

848
01:29:43,208 --> 01:29:44,625
What's the matter, Ratna?

849
01:29:54,875 --> 01:29:55,958
Ratna.

850
01:29:57,333 --> 01:30:00,291
If this is about the stupid guy,
just forget him.

851
01:30:02,916 --> 01:30:04,375
-Ratna--
-Shut up.

852
01:30:24,500 --> 01:30:26,625
When can I join the art school?

853
01:30:31,583 --> 01:30:33,166
Whenever you want.

854
01:30:34,041 --> 01:30:35,250
As soon as possible.

855
01:31:02,458 --> 01:31:03,666
Do you remember?

856
01:31:05,083 --> 01:31:06,833
We would race after school.

857
01:31:08,791 --> 01:31:09,958
Sometimes you win.

858
01:31:11,416 --> 01:31:12,708
Sometimes I do.

859
01:31:16,583 --> 01:31:18,666
We don't have to do this stupid race.

860
01:31:23,500 --> 01:31:24,541
Why?

861
01:31:27,666 --> 01:31:29,041
Lost your crush?

862
01:31:47,666 --> 01:31:49,791
Today's game is a "Macha Original".

863
01:35:11,166 --> 01:35:12,333
Jimmy?

864
01:35:14,500 --> 01:35:16,125
Azam.

865
01:35:16,208 --> 01:35:18,625
Jimmy, are you okay?

866
01:35:20,666 --> 01:35:21,541
Jimmy!

867
01:35:33,458 --> 01:35:34,875
Jimmy!

868
01:35:38,250 --> 01:35:39,250
Jimmy?

869
01:35:42,000 --> 01:35:42,875
Jimmy?

870
01:35:44,291 --> 01:35:45,875
-My Car.
-Hold on, Jimmy.

871
01:35:46,916 --> 01:35:50,333
Think of Allah. I told you, Jimmy.

872
01:35:50,416 --> 01:35:53,291
Why must you do this stupid thing?

873
01:35:56,083 --> 01:35:58,208
I wanted to be like you.

874
01:35:59,750 --> 01:36:02,541
There is no need for it, Jimmy.

875
01:36:03,041 --> 01:36:04,208
Call an ambulance!

876
01:36:04,791 --> 01:36:06,458
What ambulance? Call the police!

877
01:36:06,541 --> 01:36:08,166
Your friend should die!

878
01:36:10,333 --> 01:36:14,500
I'm sorry, Azam.

879
01:36:15,000 --> 01:36:18,625
I should be the one saying sorry.
I have done you a lot of wrong.

880
01:36:18,708 --> 01:36:19,791
Jimmy.

881
01:36:22,083 --> 01:36:25,166
You don't need to speak.
Just be quiet, Jimmy.

882
01:36:25,250 --> 01:36:26,625
Just leave, Azam.

883
01:36:26,708 --> 01:36:29,375
I will not leave, Jimmy.

884
01:36:29,458 --> 01:36:32,166
-I will not leave.
-Just leave!

885
01:36:32,250 --> 01:36:33,583
Hey!

886
01:36:34,708 --> 01:36:36,583
Hey, where are you going?

887
01:36:37,375 --> 01:36:39,583
Call the police.
Hurry and call the police.

888
01:36:40,416 --> 01:36:41,750
Go!

889
01:36:41,833 --> 01:36:43,416
Call the police now!

890
01:36:44,000 --> 01:36:45,000
Jimmy?

891
01:36:45,083 --> 01:36:46,875
Leave, Azam!

892
01:36:51,291 --> 01:36:52,541
Hello, Sir.

893
01:36:53,041 --> 01:36:54,500
A street racer got into an accident.

894
01:37:13,791 --> 01:37:16,458
-Hey!
-Come back!

895
01:37:16,541 --> 01:37:17,458
Hey!

896
01:38:09,166 --> 01:38:10,125
Ratna.

897
01:38:11,958 --> 01:38:14,750
You will not be alone anymore, okay?

898
01:38:21,291 --> 01:38:22,458
Azam.

899
01:38:23,500 --> 01:38:24,541
Azam?

900
01:38:26,458 --> 01:38:27,791
Azam?

901
01:38:30,333 --> 01:38:31,250
Ratna.

902
01:38:34,041 --> 01:38:35,000
Ratna.

903
01:38:36,625 --> 01:38:37,708
I'm sorry.

904
01:38:39,708 --> 01:38:42,625
I didn't mean what I said to you before.

905
01:38:48,916 --> 01:38:50,208
You were lying, right?

906
01:38:50,833 --> 01:38:52,750
You won't leave me, right?

907
01:38:56,041 --> 01:38:57,416
I was lying.

908
01:38:59,708 --> 01:39:01,125
I knew it.

909
01:39:02,583 --> 01:39:05,958
You were also lying
about returning to your hometown.

910
01:39:08,458 --> 01:39:10,041
You were lying, right?

911
01:39:14,666 --> 01:39:15,708
Azam?

912
01:39:18,333 --> 01:39:19,625
But why, Azam?

913
01:39:21,166 --> 01:39:23,958
-Why did you want to leave me so much?
-Ratna…

914
01:39:26,375 --> 01:39:27,833
If I…

915
01:39:30,333 --> 01:39:32,000
If a street racer like me…

916
01:39:34,333 --> 01:39:36,583
a scum like me…

917
01:39:39,666 --> 01:39:41,166
were to be with you,

918
01:39:42,250 --> 01:39:44,041
your life would be stuck.

919
01:39:44,125 --> 01:39:47,083
What are you talking about, Azam?

920
01:39:47,166 --> 01:39:49,583
Ratna, just go.

921
01:39:51,583 --> 01:39:52,833
Just go.

922
01:40:03,333 --> 01:40:05,041
Don't stop drawing.

923
01:40:07,125 --> 01:40:08,500
Listen to me.

924
01:40:11,208 --> 01:40:12,666
Forget about me.

925
01:40:15,333 --> 01:40:16,541
Just forget me.

926
01:41:19,875 --> 01:41:21,458
I will never forget you, Azam.

927
01:43:26,250 --> 01:43:28,541
WELCOME TO PERLIS

928
01:44:21,375 --> 01:44:22,666
You want to sell the bike?

929
01:44:30,791 --> 01:44:32,583
Take good care of it, okay?

930
01:44:37,958 --> 01:44:39,000
Thank you.

931
01:44:58,125 --> 01:44:59,708
<i>Take care of this place properly, Jet.</i>

932
01:45:05,041 --> 01:45:06,291
<i>Pursue your dream.</i>

933
01:45:22,666 --> 01:45:24,458
MAT JET MOTORSPORT
OPENING SOON

934
01:45:32,833 --> 01:45:34,625
This is our gallery.

935
01:45:34,708 --> 01:45:38,666
We display artwork
from special people like you.

936
01:45:39,500 --> 01:45:42,666
We have framed all of your artwork here.

937
01:45:43,166 --> 01:45:44,833
You're so talented.

938
01:45:49,125 --> 01:45:50,583
But why is this frame empty?

939
01:45:53,833 --> 01:45:56,041
Because the art is not with me.

940
01:46:06,916 --> 01:46:08,458
What is it called?

941
01:46:50,958 --> 01:46:52,333
<i>"The Night's Angel."</i>

942
01:50:58,958 --> 01:51:00,875
A NAZIFDIN NASRUDIN FILM
THIS IS A WORK OF FICTION

943
01:51:00,958 --> 01:51:03,041
ANY SIMILARITY TO ORGANIZATIONS OR PEOPLE
IS PURELY COINCIDENTAL